0..80 Comment "//! A family over two widths with rules: each rule keeps the width of each term."
81..84 Comment "//!"
85..162 Comment "//! The terms of a fragment stand at more than one sort: a bit and a word. An"
163..239 Comment "//! operation takes terms of some sorts and gives a term of one sort. A rule"
240..274 Comment "//! relates two terms of one sort."
275..278 Comment "//!"
279..358 Comment "//! One family over the type of the sorts holds the terms, and each constructor"
359..434 Comment "//! states its sort. The kernel reads the sort of each node of each rule. A"
435..511 Comment "//! constructor stands where its own sort does, and a variable stands at one"
512..589 Comment "//! sort on the two sides. So a rewrite of a word gives a word, and a rule of"
590..631 Comment "//! the bits rewrites a bit below a word."
632..635 Comment "//!"
636..652 Comment "//! - see: #8338"
